title: Particles from a sprite sheet
intro: A ParticleEmitter can draw a frame, or a random frame from a set, of a sprite sheet instead of squeezing the whole image into each particle.

project: Empty | Sheets

chapter: Frames | A sheet of shapes
create: Empty
rename: Chaff
add: ParticleEmitter
explain: component:ParticleEmitter | Particle Emitter | An emitter sprays small quads. With an image that is a sheet of several frames, each particle used to show the whole sheet squeezed in.
set: ParticleEmitter.Columns = 8
explain: field:ParticleEmitter.Columns | Columns | Columns and Rows cut the image into frames, as a Sprite's do.
set: ParticleEmitter.Frames = 0-1
explain: field:ParticleEmitter.Frames | Frames | Each particle picks one of these frames at random as it is born, using the game's random, so a rewound or networked game repeats exactly. Ticking Animate Frames steps through them over its life instead. Left empty, the Frame field shows one frame and everything draws as before.
